  <xs:complexType name="t_bush2">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">The tree that replaces &lt;bush&gt;: a tree whose nodes with a loaded xlink:href are the document they link to. A selection that includes such a node whose document has not loaded, whether by click, keyboard, multi-select, setSelection or set, loads that document first and lands once it has, reporting its root rather than the node's entry in the listing above it. Clicking a row selects it and opens it, and clicking the selected row again closes it. A single node selected by the process is opened. Its keys, its screen-reader semantics (each row's level and its place among its siblings, the live region beside the tree) and the way to move rows without dragging are the tree's: see Tree. A rule with can-have-children=&quot;true&quot; lets a node with an xlink:href load its children: a data node with children=&quot;false&quot; beside its xlink:href is a leaf; for a link not opened yet, a document already in the cache decides the twisty (an empty one gives none unless the rule has empty-text), otherwise the twisty stays until it loads.</xs:documentation>
